new file mode 100644
index 0000000..36d8f2f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/packages/player-execution.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# player-execution: Workflow Player Execution Context
+
+## Intent
+
+This package allows an independently hosted workflow to run its configured roles against task-local files and observe authentic events without injecting adapter implementations into a CLI launcher.
+
+## External Behavior
+
+### player-execution-1
+
+When a workflow calls a configured player through the public session port, the host shall pass its explicit working directory, local attachments, native-skill selection, tool allowlist and native output schema to that invocation only, preserving configured model/service selection and the existing continuation transaction.
+An explicit `freshSession:true` with `resume:false` shall reset that role for a new task; all other calls shall retain exact ledger continuation checks.
+The host shall reject any requested permission capability beyond the configured role ceiling before dispatch, allow a narrower policy, and leave omitted settings unchanged.
+
+### player-execution-2
+
+When the workflow observes an invocation through `onEvent`, the host shall await the observer after recording each authentic player event and propagate observer failure without fabricating a successful result.
+The host shall expose the effective configured adapter/model/effort in the role binding without copying credentials.
+
+## Verification
+
+### player-execution-3
+
+When system tests drive a standalone workflow through the standard CLI with real local-file tools and separate roles, they shall verify the actual working directory, explicit role model, bounded permissions, attachment delivery and continuation behavior [[player-execution-1](#player-execution-1)] and compare observed events with the durable official player journal [[player-execution-2](#player-execution-2)].
